{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>With mighty wrestlings I have wrestled.</b> From the expression צָמִיד פָּתִיל (Numbers 19:15) — divine and holy bondings did I forge with my husband." "<b>with my sister.</b> And this I did together with my sister: we brought our rivals into our homes together, in order to establish tribes. For indeed Leah gave Zilpah to Jacob of necessity before Naphtali was born, since in seven years eight tribes were born: six sons of Leah and two sons of Zilpah. And when we reckon nine months for each pregnancy, that is seventy-two months, which are six years, besides the nine months of pregnancy with Dan, which preceded all the pregnancies of the eight tribes. From all this it follows that Leah gave Zilpah to Jacob before the birth of Naphtali, for otherwise the seven years would not suffice for all their pregnancies — unless we say they were all born at seven months and conceived immediately upon giving birth and did not observe any impurity of childbirth." "<b>and I prevailed.</b> I achieved what I desired in the matter of giving my handmaid to my husband."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:32:28.862062347Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}